re-checkout, session artifact not project source. Corroborates Phase-1 auditor's independent sweep.\n\n[4] PLACEMENT/FORMATTING CONSISTENCY — PASS.\n- Identical pattern all four: '## SHELL COMMAND MECHANICS' + blank + single short paragraph + blank, immediately after frontmatter close + blank, before the file's h1. Deny-trio texts identical except deliberate per-file frontmatter-quoting mirroring and role-appropriate examples.\n\n[5] #417 PART 1 ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA — MET. Short role-matched sections appended below frontmatter in exactly the four agent files; zero frontmatter changes; no out-of-scope edits; committed as 8f997b1b referencing [#417]. Part 2 (MCP permission semantics) correctly absent - deferred per 19:04 intervention to #425.\n\n### SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n- .opencode/agents/builder.md:19 — 'enforced by by_type hook': literally, builder's gated_git_commands lives at agent_overrides top level (by_type.builder carries only allowed_bash_prefixes; crosslink-guard.ts:434 replaces defaults only when the by_type key is present). Behavioral claim is correct; attribution shorthand matches SESSION-START.md §1b convention. Optional precision tweak: 'enforced by crosslink-guard (agent_overrides gating)'.\n\n### NITS\n- All four files — '## SHELL COMMAND MECHANICS' (h2) precedes each file's '# <ROLE> AGENT' (h1): unusual markdown hierarchy, but uniform across all four and arguably intentional as a frontmatter-adjacent mechanics block. No action required.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\n- Per-file quoting fidelity (orchestrator '\"*\": \"deny\"' vs reviewer/auditor '\"*\": deny') shows the builder actually read each frontmatter before writing, per the hard rule.\n- Role-scoped example commands are all within each role's actual allowlist - a consumer can act on them without hitting denial.\n- Scope discipline was absolute: +4 lines/file, nothing else, matching the scope-tight relaunch mandate exactly.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED (this verdict): committed tree of 8f997b1b no